                    },
                    "message": "btw We could do this without sed\n`route_new=\"${route//metric [0-9]*/}`\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-google/networking/gbmc-bridge/gbmc-br-gw-src.sh",
                    "line": 67,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "William A. Kennington III",
                        "email": "wak@google.com",
                        "username": "wak-google"
                    },
                    "message": "We could also just ignore it like we do for the source route. `iproute2` will always use the last identifier when rebuilding the route. So appending the new metric doesn't require you to delete the old one from the string."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-google/networking/gbmc-bridge/gbmc-br-gw-src.sh",
